==Battleground==
*1 [[Puffsley's Comet]] spawns as the boss after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*3 [[Corporal Weyland]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 40~50 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,500f</sup>.
*1 [[Project A]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*4 [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*4 [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*4 [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 160 seconds<sup>4,800f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 206.67 seconds<sup>6,200f</sup>, delay 40~50 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Due to the massive buffs on the [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]] (particularly the Star Pengs), it is highly recommended if not outright required to max out all your [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] before attempting this stage. Even missing one Treasure set will lead to each Star Peng having '''672,000''' health and '''36,000''' attack power, making them nigh-unbeatable without a cheese strategy or certain [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]].

The [[Enigma Fruit]] Treasures also help greatly, allowing [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] and other units with massive damage to [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] to deal up to 33% more damage (Chill Cat's Cost Down [[Talents|Talent]] is mandatory) and to allow [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] to barely survive Puffsley's Comet's attack if upgraded to level 40. Speaking of which, Catellite is one of your best friends here, being able to absorb 3~5 Star Peng hits depending on level. Use it with [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] as meatshields. [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] are also great damage units, with Maglev being able to rush forward and hit twice when warped.

There are 3 main ways to play this stage:

#Survive and kill the initial 12 main Star Pengs using whatever units you may have, such as Catellite, Chill Cat, Can Can Cat and Maglev Cat, then finish off the supporting enemies. Shown in the first video under "Walkthrough".
#Cheese the stage using [[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer Cat CC]]. Shown in the second video.
#Use [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] or one of the Ubers listed below to lure and kill / severely damage Puffsley's Comet before support company arrives, making him a lot easier to fight.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
The following Uber Rares/[[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rares]] are good for this stage, and if you have any of these, using them will make things easier.

*[[Bora (Uber Rare Cat)|Bazibastra]]: Bazibastra has exceptional offense and defense against Aliens, allowing it to both lay a dent in Puffsley as well as soak up some hits, and having a low cooldown makes it disposable and even stackable. With a high enough level and attack up combos you could kill Puffsley's Comet in 3-4 hits! Make sure to keep it at a distance from the [[Cat Base]], as Puffsley's Comet's Omni Strike may still hit said base.
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: Greater Balrog's extreme damage with Talents makes him very useful in getting rid of Star Pengs, and his short recharge time makes it easy to get him back when necessary. Puffsley's long backswing gives him a few opportunities to strike, which can make all the difference, and when strengthened at higher levels, can cripple Puffsley in even one hit. However, his low range means you must support him with [[:Category:Cats with Warp Immunity|Warp-immune units]] to keep the Star Pengs from hitting him.
*[[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Megaphrodite]]: The classic Alien [[:Category:Nuker-class Cats|nuker]]. She can make quick work of Puffsley's Comet as well as control a ton of the Alien support. Be careful to stall Puffsley's Comet so he doesn't enter Aphrodite's blind spot.
*[[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Sharpshooter Saki]]: Serves the same purpose as Aphrodite, but with a lower cooldown and less DPS, and her Target Only ability doesn't matter in this stage, as it is purely Aliens anyway.
*[[Lumina (Legend Rare Cat)|Luminalia]]: A high level Luminalia is effectively invincible on this stage, being immune to warp and halving enemy damage with 100% uptime. Be careful, however - it still gets knocked back by Puffsley's Comet so you can still lose if Luminalia gets pushed behind your own base.
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]]: This unit can outrange all enemies in the stage (720 range - Puffsley's Omni Strike hits up to 550, whereas Corporal Weyland's Long Distance hits up to 600) and deals extreme damage, melting the durable peons and the boss quickly. You'll need to use lots of support and pair it with [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] due to its single-target attacks, so it gets the chance to kill off the annoying enemies.
*[[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Mad Doctor Klay]]: Attacks only Aliens in an Alien-only stage. Make sure to avoid hitting Puffsley's Comet and triggering his attacks, as the knockback effect can easily displace this unit. While Klay might not be able to solo Puffsley, he definitely makes dealing with Puffsley and the support much easier.
*[[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion the Ancient]]: Ganglion is strong against Aliens and can deal some serious damage, as well as being able to hit the backline with his Long Distance if positioned correctly. Because most of his attack delay consists of backswing, he can easily abuse the Warp and Knockback effects of the enemies to reset his animation. Just make sure to watch your money before you send him out, as he's pretty expensive and may leave you without enough funds to deploy meatshields.
*[[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]]: Resists Aliens, is immune to warp, destroys [[Barrier]]s at a 100% chance and creates level 4 [[Wave Attack]]s. Chips down the backline and Puffsley's Comet, as well as tanking a lot of hits from the boss. Its recharge time is quite fast for a tank, so you'd often have more out if and when the first one is destroyed. Gravolodon doesn't work alone and the enemy waves can constantly reset Puffsley's backswing, so pick your support wisely.
*[[Voli (Uber Rare Cat)|Gigavolta]]: Can easily keep the Star Pengs and Puffsley's Comet at bay with its powerful Freeze, as well as having the health and warp immunity to survive a few hits. Its recharge time and cost aren't bad either, so if it goes down early, another will be ready soon.
*[[Doktor Heaven (Legend Rare Cat)|Doktor Heaven/Professor Abyss]]: This unit targets Aliens and has good range, with Insanely Tough/Insane Damage abilities depending on form that allows her to serve as either a tank or attacker. However, as she lacks any Immunities and has a very long recharge time, she works far better as an attacker, especially considering that Professor Abyss can two-shot Puffsley's Comet.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Daybreaker Izanagi]]: With their insane damage against traited enemies and decent health, Izanagi can solely demolish Puffsley's Comet. Just make sure to bring Starting Money UP [[Cat Combo]]s like [[Bouncing Four (Combo)|Bouncing Four]] or a Rich Cat. Then finish off the rest of the enemies with your other units.

