==Trivia==
*Blue Impact may be reference to the movie ''[[wikipedia:Deep Impact (film)|Deep Impact]]'' as they have similar names and for the fact that the movie features a meteorite which is very reminiscent of Puffsley's Comet.
*Puffer Planet's Japanese name, River Pig Planet (リバーピッグプラネット), refers to how the Japanese word for pufferfish, 河豚 ''fugu'', literally translates to "river pig".
**It may also be a reference to the video game series [[wikipedia:LittleBigPlanet|''LittleBigPlanet'']] (リトルビッグプラネット), whose name is quite similar in Japanese.
*This stage was altered in [[Version 9.1 Update|Version 9.1]]. Before the update:
**Puffsley's Comet spawned after 10 seconds;
**Project A spawned after 1 minute;
**The first wave of Star Pengs appeared after 3.3 seconds and had a delay of 20-23.3 seconds between each Star Peng;
**The second wave of Star Pengs appeared after 90 seconds and had a delay of 16.7-20 seconds between each Star Peng;
**The third wave of Star Pengs appeared after 163.3 seconds and had a delay of 13.3-6.7 seconds between each Star Peng;
**The final wave of Star Pengs appeared after 223.3 seconds and had a delay of 33.3-40 seconds between each Star Peng.
*For all intents and purposes, Puffer Planet is treated as a Deadly stage, despite being labeled Merciless.
**The event poster (shown above) says, "Deadly Stage!"
**It is the only Merciless [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stage]] to award a gold [[Meow Medals|Meow Medal]] rather than platinum.
**Its [[Stage Difficulties|star difficulty]] is ★9 like most of the Deadly Advent Stages, rather than ★10 or ★11 like the Merciless ones.
**It is the only Merciless Advent Stage to be part of the limited [[Catnip Challenges]] that involve beating Advents with restrictions.
**It is the only Merciless Advent Stage to be part of a Tier 1 [[:Category:Advent Stages#Sequential Advent Stages|Sequential Advent Stage]], appearing as a [[Continuation Stage]] in [[The Dead & The Bloated]].
**Puffsley's Comet is the only Merciless [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Boss]] to appear in [[Heavenly Tower]] and [[Infernal Tower]], which otherwise only contain the Deadly Advent Bosses.
***The Merciless tag may be because of the [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]]' strength magnifications, as lowering them to meet the standards of a Deadly stage would have made it too easy with all [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]].

